# =============================================================================
# DockBack — public source repository.
#
# DEFAULT-DENY: nothing is published unless it is listed below. The repo holds
# exactly what builds and runs DockBack. Notes, backups, local settings and the
# private deploy files stay on this machine, and anything new stays private
# until it is added here on purpose.
# =============================================================================

# Ignore everything at the repository root by default...
/*

# ...then publish what builds the image...
!/Dockerfile
!/.dockerignore
!/Makefile
!/.trivyignore
!/.grype.yaml
!/go.mod
!/go.sum
!/main.go
!/embed_recover.go
!/internal/
!/frontend/
!/scripts/

# ...what runs it...
!/docker-compose.yml
!/deploy/
!/.env.example

# ...and the project's front page.
!/.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/SECURITY.md
!/screenshots/

# Inside what is published: dependencies, build output, caches and test debris.
/frontend/node_modules/
/frontend/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
/internal/web/dist/
/internal/api/_app/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*~
*.swp

# Never publish these, even if a rule above is loosened later. Secret file
# types match at any depth; the private folders are pinned to the root, because
# unpinned "backup/" and "backups/" would also swallow internal/backup (the
# backup engine) and the in-app help pages under docs/content/backups.
.env
*.env
!.env.example
*.db
*.sqlite*
*.key
*.pem
*.age
/.claude/
/backup/
/data/
/backups/
/docker-compose.dev.yml
/docker-compose.prod.yml

# Private extensions compiled into this machine's builds but never published:
# app profiles for applications that belong to this deployment, not the project.
/internal/**/private_*.go
